      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. Based on the [[credential-scoping]] page:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into that environment in the first place.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before those processes start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n\nThis approach means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by reading its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only in the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.",
